# Recorded baselines are byte evidence: checkout must preserve their
# recorded line endings even when Windows enables core.autocrlf, and their
# trailing spaces and CRLF rows are data, not whitespace errors.
*.expected -text -whitespace
# The embedded units table is a byte-exact resource, not checkout text.
crates/martensite-tkernel/src/units/Units.dat -text -whitespace
# Tests compare fixtures byte for byte with include_str!, so they keep their
# bytes on every platform.
